# Pixel handoff

- Pixel is Nathan's Grok Bot art/visual agent. It can't talk to Cursor directly. It signals through GitHub PRs labeled `ready-to-test`.

## Every Nathan message
1. At the start, quietly run:
   `gh pr list --repo Nathan-Elequin/swipe --label ready-to-test --json number,title,headRefName,body`
2. Do what Nathan asked first.
3. Then, for each listed PR he hasn't already responded to in this chat, end the reply with a short "Ready to test from Pixel" note:
   - One line on what it is and why. Assume he doesn't remember the context.
   - 1–3 things to try in-game.
   - "Say 'load it' to try it." If boss-rush is already on that branch, say "it's already loaded, just press F5" instead.

## "load it"
1. If boss-rush has uncommitted work beyond `.import` / `project.godot` / `default_bus_layout.tres` churn, ask whether to save it first. If he says yes, commit and push it to its current branch. Never discard it.
2. Discard the churn, `git fetch`, check out the PR branch.
3. Run the headless `--quit` parse check.
4. Tell him: click into Godot, reload, press F5.

## "approved" on a Pixel branch
- Follow `playtest-approve.mdc` (merge into main, push, back to main, delete the branch).
- Remove the `ready-to-test` label and comment "Approved by Nathan" on the PR.

## "not yet: <reason>"
- `gh pr comment` with his words.
- Swap the label to `needs-changes`.
- Switch boss-rush back to `main`. Pixel picks it up from there.

## Who does what (advisory)
If Nathan asks Cursor for a Pixel-type job, mention once that it's usually a Pixel job. If he insists, do it.
- **Cursor (Nathan directly):** balance numbers, card/monster rules and abilities, bugs found while playing, small UI tweaks, adding cards/monsters with placeholder art, small tweaks to one existing visual, publishing to itch.
- **Pixel:** new art and animation (sprites, frames, PixelLab), screen redesigns (mockup first), big visual passes across many files (title intro, wheel monster art), visual consistency audits, repo cleanups/recovery.
